ems.  Assist marketing with analysis to support a monetary value of Intellectual Property.&#xa0;  Interface with key ASIC suppliers to understand requirements and ensure alignment in product development  Provide deep technical support and training to advance Renesas’s commercial success.&#xa0;     Must have MS in Engineering or technical equivalent.  Must have a minimum of 10 years experience in the power management industry.  Must Have experience with firmware-enabled products and powering&#xa0;large scale application- specific integrated circuit (Central processing unit&#xa0;/Graphics processing unit etc.) in the data center market is required.  Experience with multiphase DC/DC converters powering Intel/AMD/SoC systems.  Mixed-signal Integrated Circuit/System knowledge/experience.  Experience with digitally enabled power management products.  Understanding of control loop theory and its application in power converters.  Proficiency with a full complement of lab equipment including network. analyzers, oscilloscopes and waveform generators.&#xa0;  Experience with automation of lab testing.      Renesas is an embedded semiconductor solution provider driven by its Purpose ‘ To Make Our Lives Easier .’ As the industry’s leading expert in embedded processing with unmatched quality and system-level know-how, we have evolved to provide scalable and comprehensive semiconductor solutions for automotive, industrial, infrastructure, and IoT industries based on the broadest product portfolio, including High Performance Computing, Embedded Processing, Analog &amp; Connectivity, and Power. 
