 &#xa0; &#xa0; &#xa0; &#xa0; &#xa0; People &amp; Team Leadership&#xa0;   Lead, mentor, and develop a team of power supply FAEs supporting strategic AI and&#xa0;hyperscaler&#xa0;customers.&#xa0;  Coach FAEs on&#xa0;system‑level&#xa0;power thinking, executive communication, and sound technical judgment in complex customer environments.&#xa0;  Build onboarding and training plans for new college graduates and&#xa0;early‑career&#xa0;FAEs, ensuring readiness for lab work and&#xa0;customer‑facing&#xa0;engagements.&#xa0;  Conduct performance reviews and support career development across the team.&#xa0;  Guide resource allocation across accounts, balancing customer priorities, program risk, and team bandwidth.&#xa0;  Establish a&#xa0;high‑performance&#xa0;culture with clear standards for ownership, technical rigor, and execution quality. Hold the team accountable to outcomes and model the behaviors expected through disciplined,&#xa0;high‑impact&#xa0;customer engagement.&#xa0;   &#xa0; &#xa0; &#xa0; &#xa0; &#xa0; &#xa0; &#xa0; &#xa0; &#xa0; &#xa0; &#xa0; &#xa0; &#xa0; &#xa0; &#xa0; Customer, Program &amp; Strategy Leadership&#xa0;   Own technical program execution for top datacenter customers, spanning AI accelerators, server platforms, and&#xa0;high‑performance&#xa0;networking systems.&#xa0;  Partner closely with Sales and GAM leadership to align customer priorities, program sequencing, and allocation of FAE resources.&#xa0;  Maintain program visibility through clear tracking of milestones, risks, validation status, and&#xa0;next‑step&#xa0;actions.&#xa0;  Provide concise and actionable technical updates to senior leadership.&#xa0;  Collaborate with Product Line and Marketing teams to translate strategic customer power requirements into product feedback and roadmap influence.&#xa0;  Champion field insights related to&#xa0;next‑generation&#xa0;power architectures, digital multiphase solutions, and&#xa0;module‑based&#xa0;system power.&#xa0;  Coordinate technical handoffs and shared engagements across global FAE teams.&#xa0;    &#xa0;   Bachelor’s or&#xa0;Master’s degree in Electrical Engineering&#xa0;or a related technical field.&#xa0;  Significant prior experience as a Field Applications Engineer with&#xa0;hands‑on&#xa0;responsibility for power supply or power management products.&#xa0;  8+ years of experience in power electronics, digital multiphase power delivery, server or AI platform power, or related hardware systems.&#xa0;  Deep technical&#xa0;expertise&#xa0;in power modules, digital multiphase controllers, VRMs, and&#xa0;high‑current,&#xa0;low‑voltage&#xa0;conversion for datacenter platforms.&#xa0;  Strong&#xa0;lab‑based&#xa0;debug skills including use of oscilloscopes, current probes, electronic loads, and transient response analysis.&#xa0;  Demonstrated ability to&#xa0;interface directly with&#xa0;customers on complex power topics and drive issues to closure.&#xa0;  2+ years of&#xa0;people&#xa0;leadership experience in a team lead, supervisory, managerial, or equivalent player/coach role.&#xa0;  Strong communication&#xa0;skills with the ability to translate complex technical concepts to&#xa0;customer,&#xa0;executive, and internal audiences.&#xa0;Preferred Qualifications&#xa0;  Experience supporting hyperscale datacenter customers such as cloud service providers or AI accelerator companies.&#xa0;  Expertise&#xa0;in&#xa0;system‑level&#xa0;power architecture for AI or ML accelerators, CPUs, or&#xa0;high‑end&#xa0;networking platforms.&#xa0;  Familiarity with&#xa0;PMBus, telemetry systems, and digitally controlled multiphase power solutions.&#xa0;  Proven ability to manage multiple&#xa0;high‑priority&#xa0;programs simultaneously in&#xa0;fast‑moving&#xa0;customer environments.&#xa0;  Demonstrated success developing&#xa0;early‑career&#xa0;engineers and building&#xa0;high‑performance&#xa0;technical teams.&#xa0;  Strong&#xa0;cross‑functional&#xa0;leadership experience working with Product Line, Marketing, Sales, or Systems Engineering organizations.&#xa0;      The expected annual pay range for this position is $180,000K - $220,000K. This position is also eligible for bonus opportunities. Please note that final offer amount will be dependent on geographic location, applicable experience, and skillset of the candidate.  &#xa0;  &#xa0;    Renesas is an embedded semiconductor solution provider driven by its Purpose ‘ To Make Our Lives Easier .’ As the industry’s leading expert in embedded processing with unmatched quality and system-level know-how, we have evolved to provide scalable and comprehensive semiconductor solutions for automotive, industrial, infrastructure, and IoT industries based on the broadest product portfolio, including High Performance Computing, Embedded Processing, Analog &amp; Connectivity, and Power. 
