 position goes beyond traditional controlling, successful candidate will design &amp; standardize end-to-end processes, continuously optimize financials for global R&amp;D organization, enabling informed decision‑making from early concept through executive approval.   Key Responsibilities    Strategic Planning &amp; Forecasting: Lead the annual operating plan (AOP), rolling quarterly forecasts, and 3–5 year long term planning (LTP) processes across Engineering organization. Own the consolidated financial model, ensuring alignment between strategy, operational execution, and financial outcomes.  Business Partnership: Partner closely with the Engineering Executive Leadership team. Support financial planning cycles, ad-hoc analysis, capital investment decisions. Act as a bridge between technical organizations and finance, translating complexity into actionable insights  Performance Management &amp; Leadership Insights: Establish and monitor organization-wide KPIs to assess financial and operational performance. Deliver comprehensive monthly reporting packages highlighting variances versus budget and forecast, clearly articulating risks, opportunities, and recommended actions to leadership.  Capital Allocation: Provide financial modeling, valuation analysis, and due diligence supporting major capital investment decisions. Partner with senior leadership to evaluate trade-offs and optimize capital deployment in support of strategic priorities.  Corporate policy &amp; compliance  Drive the implementation &amp; standardization of corporate policies &amp; procedures across global Engineering Organization. Serve as key stakeholder to Renesas India’s Accounting &amp; Regulatory team.&#xa0;  Team Leadership &amp; Development: Foster a culture of financial excellence, intellectual rigor, and strong business partnership, ensuring the organization scales effectively with the Product Group’s growth.   Comfortable operating in ambiguous, evolving environments. Proactive, hands‑on, and capable of driving change. Ability to design and improve end to end business processes, not just analyze results.     Experience &amp; Expertise    5+ years of progressive finance experience, including at least 3 years in a senior FP&amp;A or finance leadership role within a public company environment. Strong experience in  product‑based semiconductor businesses , manufacturing, or technology‑driven environments. Semiconductor businesses, manufacturing, or technology experiences highly preferred.  Hands‑on experience with  cost modeling, investment decisions or business case evaluation   Strong working knowledge of IFRS and experience with enterprise ERP systems such as NetSuite, SAP, or Oracle.  Proven ability to support senior leadership and executive‑level decision making through clear, compelling financial storytelling  Demonstrated success operating in high-performing teams in dynamic, fast-paced environments.    Core Skills    Strong analytical and financial modeling skills  Ability to design and improve end‑to‑end business processes, not just analyze results  Experience working with financial systems, data platforms, and reporting tools  Excellent communication skills, with the ability to explain complex financial topics clearly    Education :   &#xa0;Bachelor’s degree in Finance, Accounting, Economics, or a related field is required. An MBA, CPA, or CFA is highly preferred.      Renesas is an embedded semiconductor solution provider driven by its Purpose ‘ To Make Our Lives Easier .’ As the industry’s leading expert in embedded processing with unmatched quality and system-level know-how, we have evolved to provide scalable and comprehensive semiconductor solutions for automotive, industrial, infrastructure, and IoT industries based on the broadest product portfolio, including High Performance Computing, Embedded Processing, Analog &amp; Connectivity, and Power. 
