This role is responsible for  leading  MLCC/ inductor/ Embedded substrate  strategic sourcing  and  commercial management , driving cost optimization, ensuring supply continuity, and owning end-to-end supplier strategy. The role requires strong leadership, program management, and cross-functional influence to align business, engineering, and supply chain objectives while driving  long-term  value creation.  ________________________________________  Key Responsibilities  • Lead commercial negotiations including pricing, LTAs, capacity agreements, price adjustments, and payment terms for MLCC/inductors/ Embedded substrates.  • Own supplier strategy for MLCC/ inductor/ Embedded substrate commodities, acting as a key decision driver in supplier selection and allocation.  • Drive cost optimization initiatives using structured methodologies such as cost breakdown analysis, should-cost modeling, and localization strategies.  • Lead cross-functional engagement with Engineering and Product Groups to ensure component readiness and alignment across NPI, ramp-up, and lifecycle management.  • Ensure supply continuity and resilience by proactively managing capacity planning, allocation strategies, and long-term supply assurance with key component suppliers.  • Identify, assess, and mitigate supply chain risks including capacity constraints, geopolitical exposure, cost volatility, and supplier dependency within the passive/component supply base.  • Lead contract governance including MSA, NDA, pricing frameworks, and commercial agreements, ensuring alignment with business strategy.  • Drive supplier performance management through structured reviews, KPI tracking, and continuous improvement initiatives.  • Lead escalation of management and resolution of critical issues related to quality, delivery, capacity, and commercial disputes.  • Act as a strategic interface between internal functions (Engineering, Product Group, Supply Chain, and Finance teams) and MLCC / inductor / substrate suppliers to ensure alignment on roadmap, cost, and execution priorities.   •  10+&#xa0; years  of purchasing/procurement experience, preferably in the semiconductor or electronics industry.  • Fluent in English is required; Japanese language proficiency is a plus.  • Hands-on experience or strong familiarity with passive components (MLCC/ inductors/ Embedded substrate) is a strong advantage.  • Advanced Excel and data analysis skills; proficient in PowerPoint for executive-level presentations.  • Strong stakeholder management, communication, and negotiation skills with the ability to influence cross-functional teams and senior stakeholders.  • Experience in strategic sourcing, supplier management, or program management is highly preferred.     Renesas is an embedded semiconductor solution provider driven by its Purpose ‘ To Make Our Lives Easier .’ As the industry’s leading expert in embedded processing with unmatched quality and system-level know-how, we have evolved to provide scalable and comprehensive semiconductor solutions for automotive, industrial, infrastructure, and IoT industries based on the broadest product portfolio, including High Performance Computing, Embedded Processing, Analog &amp; Connectivity, and Power. 
