cal skills, measured through manager review.  Demonstrate ability to build effective relationships with relevant stakeholders.  Display enthusiasm, drive, confidence and team work in the role      Entry Level - Electrical Engineering or related field.&#xa0; Bachelor's degree with up to 2 years of experience or recent master's grad with no experience.&#xa0; Master's applicants preferred.    Applicants for this position must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Renesas is unable to sponsor applicants for work visas for this position now or in the future. &#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;  Knowledge of&#xa0;CMOS Analog and switch mode power supplies SMPS  Apply policy/procedures to resolve routine issues  Desire for continued learning and development  Cross cultural awareness and sensitivity  Results-oriented and able to deliver on-time under tight schedules  Ability to work both independently and as part of a team  Flexible to undertake occasional international travel at short notice  Excellent command of verbal and written English  Ability to propose innovative solutions  Concise and precise communication and presentation skills within multi-site and multi-cultural environment      Renesas is an embedded semiconductor solution provider driven by its Purpose ‘ To Make Our Lives Easier .’ As the industry’s leading expert in embedded processing with unmatched quality and system-level know-how, we have evolved to provide scalable and comprehensive semiconductor solutions for automotive, industrial, infrastructure, and IoT industries based on the broadest product portfolio, including High Performance Computing, Embedded Processing, Analog &amp; Connectivity, and Power. 
