entive actions.  Create and maintain accurate network documentation, diagrams, standards, runbooks, and standard operational procedures.  Stay current with AWS networking services, cloud security practices, automation methods, and industry best practices, and recommend improvements where appropriate.     Required Skills    Bachelor's degree in computer science, Information technology or related field  5+ years of hands-on experience in designing, implementing and supporting AWS cloud networking solutions  AWS Certified Advanced Networking - Specialty is desirable  Hands-on experience with AWS networking services, including VPC, Transit Gateway, Direct Connect, VPNs, Route 53, Elastic Load Balancing, route tables, VPC endpoints, security groups, and network ACLs.  Strong knowledge of core networking concepts and protocols, including TCP/IP, DNS, DHCP, routing, subnetting, NAT, VPN, BGP, and OSPF.  Deep understanding of network security concepts, including network segmentation, firewalls, WAF, access control, encryption in transit, traffic inspection, and secure hybrid connectivity.  Experience with Infrastructure as Code and automation tools, preferably Terraform, with the ability to create reusable, maintainable, and version-controlled network configurations.  Experience with network monitoring, logging, and troubleshooting tools such as AWS CloudWatch, VPC Flow Logs, CloudTrail, or similar platforms.  Strong analytical and troubleshooting skills, with the ability to debug complex network issues in a timely manner.  Excellent verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to produce clear documentation, diagrams, and operational procedures.  Strong ownership mindset, positive attitude, and ability to work effectively in a collaborative team environment.      Renesas is an embedded semiconductor solution provider driven by its Purpose,  To Make Our Lives Easier . With a global team of over 21,000 engineers and problem solvers in more than 30 countries, we 