At Renesas, we are more than just a semiconductor company; we are the engine behind a "safer, smarter, and more sustainable" future. Headquartered locally in the heart of San Jose, our Silicon Valley team is at the forefront of innovation in Automotive, Industrial, Infrastructure, and IoT technologies. By blending cutting-edge embedded processing with world-class analog and power expertise, we develop "Winning Combinations" that power billions of intelligent devices globally. Joining our San Jose office means joining a collaborative, forward-thinking environment where your work directly impacts the next generation of AI-driven infrastructure and green energy solutions.   Sr. Staff application engineer for position in HiRel product group. Primary responsibilities will include supporting existing analog products as well as new product developments for the space market. Products supported include: Precision Op-amps, Instrumentation Amplifiers, Voltage References, Precision ADCs, Battery Management Systems (BMS), Analog Switches/Multiplexers, Current Sources and Drivers, Isolators, and Serial Interface (i.e. RS-422, CANBUS, I2C). Programming experience with Python, Java, and/or C languages as well as knowledge of Verilog coding with FPGAs a plus. Knowledge of using and troubleshooting PSpice models.&#xa0;&#xa0;   You will be part of an engineering team responsible for device characterization, datasheet and application note documentation, and customer support.&#xa0;&#xa0;  Work in a multi-disciplinary New Product Development engineering team to help define, evaluate, characterize, and document new product developments with the goal of bringing products to the marketplace.&#xa0;  Engage with potential customers in support of FAE or Marketing / Sales visits or conference calls to help refine their application needs into deliverable product features for future product definitions.&#xa0;  Support customer needs as they implement our products into their hardware systems via email, conference calls, or on-site visits.&#xa0;  Participate in global industry conventions as a presenter.&#xa0;   &#xa0; 
RESPONSIBILITIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: &#xa0; 
&#xa0; 
The Applications Engineering position will be responsible for three main functions: &#xa0; 
&#xa0; 
Device Characterization (50% of time): &#xa0; 
You will work with a very talented team of Engineers to perform various lab tests for the characterization of the different products. Prepare the validation plan and compile validation reports upon complete of bench testing/characterization. It is important to understand how the parts are tested to be able to understand their performance when assisting customers. This knowledge will aid in setting up the customer’s exact configuration for verification and characterization of a customer’s issue.&#xa0;&#xa0;  Documentation (20% of time): &#xa0; 
You will utilize FrameMaker for generating and editing Data Sheets and then work with the Technical Documentation to publish them. You will be expected to keep accurate lab notes (software of your choice) and document any test procedures for future reference. As you progress in your learning, you will be expected to generate and publish Technical Briefs, Application Notes, Customers Responses, and possibly Articles. &#xa0; 
&#xa0; 
Customer Support (20% of time): &#xa0; 
You will work with marketing and sales to facilitate the design-in of our products as well as provide technical assistance to address customer questions and analyze field returns. You will train Field Application Engineers on products and demonstrations systems to enhance sales channel effectiveness.&#xa0;&#xa0;  New Product Definition (10%)&#xa0;  Work with Marketing, Customer, Design and Product engineering teams to help define new products.   JOB REQUIREMENTS/ QUALIFICATIONS: &#xa0; 
Need for candidate is time sensitive and therefore preferred to be a US citizen or have a green card.&#xa0;  Candidate must possess a minimum bachelor’s degree (or equivalent) in Electrical/Electronic Engineering.&#xa0;  Candidate should be self-motivated and conscientious.&#xa0;  Candidate must have excellent verbal and written communication skills.&#xa0;&#xa0;  Candidate must have good presentation skills.&#xa0;  Candidate should have a good knowledge of analog design and lab troubleshooting skills.&#xa0;  Candidate must understand and follow industry standards of test for ICs.&#xa0;  &#xa0;  Required Skills: &#xa0; 
7 to 10+ Years in Applications and/or Systems Engineering role in Analog IC Development or Circuit Design Industry.&#xa0;  Proficient with analog and mixed signal designs.&#xa0;  Proficient with electronic bench lab equipment (power supplies, function generators, multi-meters, oscilloscopes).&#xa0;  Experience in Schematic/Layout design tools and switching power supply layout concepts (Altium preferred).&#xa0;  Familiar with Microsoft Office (Excel, Power Point).&#xa0;  Experience writing programming code (i.e. Python) to automate lab bench equipment in GBIP/USB communication a plus.&#xa0;  Experience modeling circuits (SPICE and or IBIS) is desired but not mandatory.&#xa0;  &#xa0;  &#xa0;     Renesas is an embedded semiconductor solution provider driven by its Purpose,  To Make Our Lives Easier . With a global team of over 21,000 engineers and problem solvers in more than 30 countries, we offer the opportunity to work on world‑leading technology for Automotive, Industrial, Infrastructure, and IoT, shaping a safer, healthier, greener, and smarter future.  At Renesas, TAGIE is our culture, grounded in being Transparent, Agile, Global, Innovative, and Entrepreneurial. It shapes how we work, grow and deliver on our purpose together. This collaborative spirit and mindset drive our semiconductor technology to transform industries and impact millions of lives.  We believe in rewarding our employees with a competitive benefits package alongside their salary. More information will be provided during the hiring process.  Are you ready to join our team and  shape the future  with us?  Renesas Electronics is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer, committed to supporting diversity and fostering a work environment free of discrimination on the basis of sex, race, religion, national origin, gender, gender identity, gender expression, age, sexual orientation, military status, veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. For more information, please read our&#xa0; Diversity &amp; Inclusion Statement .  Renesas Electronics deals with dual-use technology that is subject to U.S. export controls regulations. Under these regulations it may be necessary for Renesas to obtain U.S. government export license prior to release of technology to certain persons. The decision whether or not to file or pursue an export license application is at the sole discretion of Renesas.

Renesas is one of the top global semiconductor companies in the world. We strive to develop a safer, healthier, greener, and smarter world, and our goal is to make every endpoint intelligent by offering product solutions in the automotive, industrial, infrastructure and IoT markets. Our robust product portfolio includes world leading MCUs, SoCs, Analog and power products, plus Winning Combination solutions that curate these complementary products. We are a key supplier to the world’s leading manufacturers of electronics you rely on every day; you may not see our products, but they are all around you.  Renesas employs roughly 21,000 people in more than 30 countries worldwide. As a global team, our employees actively embody the Renesas Culture, our guiding principles based on five key elements: Transparent, Agile, Global, Innovative, and Entrepreneurial. Renesas believes in, and has a commitment to, diversity and inclusion, with initiatives and a leadership team dedicated to its resources and values. At Renesas, we want to build a sustainable future where technology helps make our lives easier. Join us and build your future by being part of what’s next in electronics and the world.   Job Description  Renesas is looking for a Principal Engineer, Validation. to redefine how automotive‑grade silicon quality is built—driving first‑time‑right silicon, eliminating customer escapes, and setting a new industry benchmark for validation excellence  &#xa0; Key Responsibilities    Define and own the end‑to‑end silicon validation strategy for automotive and HPC SoCs, from pre‑silicon enablement through post‑silicon production release.  Ensure first‑time‑right silicon, robust validation coverage, and zero customer escapes across all assigned programs.  Lead global validation teams responsible for silicon bring‑up, characterization, and system‑level validation across multiple concurrent programs.  Establish and drive a System Use Case Validation Program, harvesting real customer/OEM and system scenarios and converting them into automated, traceable validation suites.  Influence SoC architecture, design, and program decisions through early validation insights, risk identification, and data‑backed recommendations.  Drive shift‑left validation as a measurable engineering program, increasing reuse across simulation, emulation/FPGA, and silicon to reduce late surprises.  Own escape‑prevention strategy, including robustness testing, fault scenarios, coverage models, and disciplined validation signoff criteria.  Build and scale high‑performing validation organizations, developing strong technical leadership (Staff/Principal pipeline) and execution ownership.  Lead automation, standardization, and infrastructure modernization across validation labs, board farms, and CI systems.  Establish validation methodologies, quality benchmarks, metrics, and dashboards aligned with Renesas standards and automotive expectations.  Identify technical, execution, and program risks early; drive data‑driven mitigation and executive decision‑making.  Provide clear executive‑level reporting on validation status, risks, readiness, and outcomes.  Act as a trusted partner to Design, DV, Test, Firmware, Software, Product Engineering, Quality, and BU leadership.  Adoption of industry best practices as a measurable program   &#xa0;    Required Skills &amp; Experience    B.E./B. Tech or M.E./M. Tech in Electronics, Electrical, or Computer Engineering, or equivalent industry experience.  16+ years of experience in semiconductor validation, characterization, or silicon engineering, with demonstrated ownership of silicon quality outcomes.  Strong domain expertise in automotive SoC validation, system‑level use‑case testing, and robustness validation.  Proven experience delivering complex SoC programs from first silicon through production release.  Deep understanding of silicon validation flows, lab environments, and post‑silicon debug ecosystems.  Demonstrated success building and scaling automation‑first validation frameworks using Python, C++, or similar technologies.  Strong experience driving cross‑functional execution in a matrixed, global environment.  Excellent executive communication, stakeholder management, and decision‑making skills.  Experience with AI frameworks for SoC Validation efficiency and quality gain— eg validation specific AI agents, Cody AI for content development etc.    Preferred    Experience with ISO 26262 / ASIL‑D development and validation environments.  Exposure to emulation/FPGA‑based shift‑left validation and pre↔post silicon continuity models.  Strong foundation in mixed‑signal and digital silicon validation, including pattern‑based and system‑level methodologies.  Track record of institutionalizing industry best practices across multiple programs and organizations.  Experience leading culture change toward proactive risk ownership, evidence‑based closure, and challenge‑ready execution.  Automotive OEM or Tier‑1 customer engagement experience.    Renesas is an embedded semiconductor solution provider driven by its Purpose ‘ To Make Our Lives Easier .’ As the industry’s leading expert in embedded processing with unmatched quality and system-level know-how, we have evolved to provide scalable and comprehensive semiconductor solutions for automotive, industrial, infrastructure, and IoT industries based on the broadest product portfolio, including High Performance Computing, Embedded Processing, Analog &amp; Connectivity, and Power. 
&#xa0; 
With a diverse team of over 21,000 professionals in more than 30 countries, we continue to expand our boundaries to offer enhanced user experiences through digitalization and usher into a new era of innovation. We design and develop sustainable, power-efficient solutions today that help people and communities thrive tomorrow, ‘ To Make Our Lives Easier .’&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0; &#xa0; 
&#xa0; 
At Renesas, you can:&#xa0;    Launch and advance your career&#xa0; in technical and business roles across four Product Groups and various corporate functions. You will have the opportunities to explore our hardware and software capabilities and try new things.&#xa0;&#xa0;     Make a real impact&#xa0; by developing innovative products and solutions to meet our global customers' evolving needs and help make people’s lives easier, safe and secure.&#xa0;     Maximize your performance and wellbeing &#xa0;in our flexible and inclusive work environment. Our people-first culture and global support system, including the remote work option and Employee Resource Groups, will help you excel from the first day.&#xa0;&#xa0; &#xa0;   Are you ready to own your success and make your mark? &#xa0;  Join Renesas. Let’s&#xa0; Shape the Future&#xa0; together.&#xa0;&#xa0;  Renesas Electronics is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer, committed to supporting diversity and fostering a work environment free of discrimination on the basis of sex, race, religion, national origin, gender, gender identity, gender expression, age, sexual orientation, military status, veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. For more information, please read our&#xa0; Diversity &amp; Inclusion Statement .  We have adopted a hybrid model that gives employees the ability to work remotely two days a week while ensuring that we come together as a team in the office the rest of the time. The designated in-office days are Tuesday through Thursday for innovation, collaboration and continuous learning.    Renesas is an embedded semiconductor solution provider driven by its Purpose,  To Make Our Lives Easier . With a global team of over 21,000 engineers and problem solvers in more than 30 countries, we offer the opportunity to work on world‑leading technology for Automotive, Industrial, Infrastructure, and IoT, shaping a safer, healthier, greener, and smarter future.  At Renesas, TAGIE is our culture, grounded in being Transparent, Agile, Global, Innovative, and Entrepreneurial. It shapes how we work, grow and deliver on our purpose together. This collaborative spirit and mindset drive our semiconductor technology to transform industries and impact millions of lives.  We believe in rewarding our employees with a competitive benefits package alongside their salary. More information will be provided during the hiring process.  Are you ready to join our team and  shape the future  with us?  Renesas Electronics is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer, committed to supporting diversity and fostering a work environment free of discrimination on the basis of sex, race, religion, national origin, gender, gender identity, gender expression, age, sexual orientation, military status, veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. For more information, please read our&#xa0; Diversity &amp; Inclusion Statement .

Renesas is one of the top global semiconductor companies in the world. We strive to develop a safer, healthier, greener, and smarter world, and our goal is to make every endpoint intelligent by offering product solutions in the automotive, industrial, infrastructure and IoT markets. Our robust product portfolio includes world-leading MCUs, SoCs, analog and power products, plus Winning Combination solutions that curate these complementary products. We are a key supplier to the world’s leading manufacturers of electronics you rely on every day; you may not see our products, but they are all around you. &#xa0;  Renesas employs roughly 21,000 people in more than 30 countries worldwide. As a global team, our employees actively embody the Renesas Culture, our guiding principles based on five key elements: Transparent, Agile, Global, Innovative, and Entrepreneurial. Renesas believes in, and has a commitment to, diversity and inclusion, with initiatives and a leadership team dedicated to its resources and values. At Renesas, we want to build a sustainable future where technology helps make our lives easier. Join us and build your future by being part of what’s next in electronics and the world.    &#xa0; Key Responsibilities    Define and own the end‑to‑end silicon validation strategy for automotive and HPC SoCs, from pre‑silicon enablement through post‑silicon production release.  Ensure first‑time‑right silicon, robust validation coverage, and zero customer escapes across all assigned programs.  Lead global validation teams responsible for silicon bring‑up, characterization, and system‑level validation across multiple concurrent programs.  Establish and drive a System Use Case Validation Program, harvesting real customer/OEM and system scenarios and converting them into automated, traceable validation suites.  Influence SoC architecture, design, and program decisions through early validation insights, risk identification, and data‑backed recommendations.  Drive shift‑left validation as a measurable engineering program, increasing reuse across simulation, emulation/FPGA, and silicon to reduce late surprises.  Own escape‑prevention strategy, including robustness testing, fault scenarios, coverage models, and disciplined validation signoff criteria.  Build and scale high‑performing validation organizations, developing strong technical leadership (Staff/Principal pipeline) and execution ownership.  Lead automation, standardization, and infrastructure modernization across validation labs, board farms, and CI systems.  Establish validation methodologies, quality benchmarks, metrics, and dashboards aligned with Renesas standards and automotive expectations.  Identify technical, execution, and program risks early; drive data‑driven mitigation and executive decision‑making.  Provide clear executive‑level reporting on validation status, risks, readiness, and outcomes.  Act as a trusted partner to Design, DV, Test, Firmware, Software, Product Engineering, Quality, and BU leadership.  Adoption of industry best practices as a measurable program     Required Skills &amp; Experience    B.E./B. Tech or M.E./M. Tech in Electronics, Electrical, or Computer Engineering, or equivalent industry experience.  10 to 16&#xa0;years of experience in semiconductor validation, characterization, or silicon engineering, with demonstrated ownership of silicon quality outcomes.  Strong domain expertise in automotive SoC validation, system‑level use‑case testing, and robustness validation.  Proven experience delivering complex SoC programs from first silicon through production release.  Deep understanding of silicon validation flows, lab environments, and post‑silicon debug ecosystems.  Demonstrated success building and scaling automation‑first validation frameworks using Python, C++, or similar technologies.  Strong experience driving cross‑functional execution in a matrixed, global environment.  Excellent executive communication, stakeholder management, and decision‑making skills.  Experience with AI frameworks for SoC Validation efficiency and quality gain— eg validation specific AI agents, Cody AI for content development etc.    Preferred    Experience with ISO 26262 / ASIL‑D development and validation environments.  Exposure to emulation/FPGA‑based shift‑left validation and pre↔post silicon continuity models.  Strong foundation in mixed‑signal and digital silicon validation, including pattern‑based and system‑level methodologies.  Track record of institutionalizing industry best practices across multiple programs and organizations.  Experience leading culture change toward proactive risk ownership, evidence‑based closure, and challenge‑ready execution.  Automotive OEM or Tier‑1 customer engagement experience.    Renesas is an embedded semiconductor solution provider driven by its Purpose ‘ To Make Our Lives Easier .’ As the industry’s leading expert in embedded processing with unmatched quality and system-level know-how, we have evolved to provide scalable and comprehensive semiconductor solutions for automotive, industrial, infrastructure, and IoT industries based on the broadest product portfolio, including High Performance Computing, Embedded Processing, Analog &amp; Connectivity, and Power. 
&#xa0; 
With a diverse team of over 21,000 professionals in more than 30 countries, we continue to expand our boundaries to offer enhanced user experiences through digitalization and usher into a new era of innovation. We design and develop sustainable, power-efficient solutions today that help people and communities thrive tomorrow, ‘ To Make Our Lives Easier .’&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0; &#xa0; 
&#xa0; 
