&lt;p&gt;Health Care Aide - Alberta&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fort Saskatchewan Care Community&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #0e0e0e;"&gt;Rate of Pay:&nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;$23.21&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: black;"&gt;This posting is for an existing vacancy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: black;"&gt;.&nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Sienna you won&rsquo;t just fill a position; you will build lasting relationships with residents who call Fort Saskatchewan Care Community their home.&nbsp; &nbsp;Join us in a role where knowing each resident not just by name, but by story, is not just possible, it is expected.&nbsp; &nbsp;Our purpose is to cultivate happiness in daily life!&nbsp; We truly believe it is a privilege to serve Canada&rsquo;s seniors, ensuring they live fulfilling lives with the utmost comfort, dignity, and respect.&nbsp;&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to a Wellness Manager, the Health Care Aide is a critical role within our communities as it impacts the lives of residents.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If this resonates with you, please keep reading&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What Sienna Offers:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a purpose driven organization.&nbsp; We aspire to cultivate an environment and culture where team members feel valued, heard and empowered to do meaningful work.&nbsp; And we offer a number of programs and benefits that support team members&rsquo; financial, personal and professional needs:&nbsp;&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; A competitive salary and vacation package&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; Health &amp; Dental benefits program&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; Share Ownership and Reward Program (SOAR)&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; Employee Share Purchase Plan with company match&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; Continuous learning and growth so you have the skillset needed to succeed and take on new challenges&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; A welcoming culture that values diversity and differing perspectives, experiences and beliefs&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&nbsp;What You&rsquo;ll Be Doing:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be a welcomed member of the Long Term Care team at Fort Saskatchewan Care Community, working in a fast-paced environment where you will make a meaningful difference in residents&rsquo; lives.&nbsp; As a Health Care Aide, you&rsquo;ll form a deep understanding of your residents and their living experience.&nbsp; You will build relationships with the residents and their family members, offering a variety of support options and program choices that enrich their daily health and well being. As an individual and part of a wider team, you will be a strong contributor to the culture of the home, where the focus is always on helping residents live fully, every day.&nbsp;&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;How You&rsquo;ll Succeed:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;1. Provide Resident Supervision and Assistance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; support residents with their activities of daily living including eating, dressing, hygiene and grooming as per residents&rsquo; individual plans of care&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;2. Provide Resident Care and Services&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; aid residents with respect to their communication and connections by encouraging them to wear individual sensory aids such as glasses, hearing aides, etc.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; with additional prescribed training, administer specific medication to residents under the supervision of a registered health professional&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; ensure residents have constant and easy access to mobility or assistive devices such as canes, walkers, call bells, etc.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;3. Support Resident Comfort &amp; Well-being&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; provide ongoing cognitive, social, emotional, and spiritual support; as well as oral and dental care&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; encourage residents to participate in programs offered by the Resident Experience Team, whether individual or in groups&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; You are compassionate and dedicated to meaningful work that supports seniors in living life fully&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; You have completed a Health Care Aide program from an approved college&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; You are detailed-oriented and proficient in procedures and techniques involved in administering simple treatment and can provide bedside care to residents&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; You exercise tact and diplomacy in working with seniors, their families and general visitors&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What you need to know:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; Sienna Senior Living is committed to creating an inclusive environment where all team members and residents feel like they belong. We seek applicants with a wide range of abilities and we provide an accessible candidate experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; You must be legally eligible to work in Canada or have a valid work/study permit&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; You must successfully pass a Vulnerable Sector Check&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Apply Now if this job sounds interesting and you want to learn more!&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sienna Senior Living may utilize artificial intelligence to screen and assess applicants for this position.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="color: #494949;"&gt;Cook&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="color: #494949;"&gt;Silverthorn Community - Mississauga&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #0e0e0e;"&gt;Rate of Pay: $22.99&lt;/span&gt;&nbsp;&lt;span style="color: #0e0e0e;"&gt;(as per collective agreement)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&nbsp;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="color: black;"&gt;This posting is for an existing vacancy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are Sienna Senior Living, a publicly traded company (TSX:SIA) and one of Canada&rsquo;s leading owners and operators of seniors&rsquo; residences.&nbsp; We offer care, support, services and housing in Retirement and Long Term Care to seniors/residents and their families.&nbsp; And we truly believe it is a privilege to serve Canada&rsquo;s seniors, ensuring they live fulfilling lives with the utmost comfort, dignity and respect.&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Sienna, we empower our team members to help our residents live the life they desire and deserve.&nbsp; We provide our team members the tools and support to deliver excellent clinical care and elevate the resident experience through choice, personalization, and community engagement.&nbsp;&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If this resonates with you, please keep reading!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Sienna Offers:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a purpose driven organization.&nbsp; We aspire to cultivate an environment and culture where team members feel valued, heard and empowered to do meaningful work.&nbsp; And we offer a number of programs and benefits that support team members&rsquo; financial, personal and professional needs:&nbsp;&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; A competitive salary and vacation package&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; Health &amp; Dental benefits program&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; RRSP with employer match&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; Share Ownership and Reward Program (SOAR)&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; Employee Share Purchase Plan with company match&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; Continuous learning and growth so you have the skillset needed to succeed and take on new challenges&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; A welcoming culture that values diversity and differing perspectives, experiences and beliefs&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a Cook your typical day will impact in the following ways:&nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; Setting up equipment and supplies for food preparation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; Preparing meals and snacks according to production sheets, recipes and other menu document as provided&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; Providing for prescribed diets, at appropriate temperatures and in portion controlled quantities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; Monitoring quality of food supplies received and advises team leader of problems and makes recommendations about corrective action&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; In the absence of the team leader, assumes responsibility for departmental operations including enu changes as necessary, requisitions and purchases food and other supplies from authorized suppliers&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; Assisting in the orientation and training of new team members&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; Performing other duties as assigned&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must haves:&nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&bull; Grade 12 minimum education required&lt;/p&gt;
