## Position Overview

At InField Scientific, our team of engineers and scientists work together to provide electromagnetic (EM) expertise and analysis to support the design and in-service support of navy ships. We work closely with governments and large multinational companies to analyze, assess and test shipboard electromagnetic environments (EME) focusing on electromagnetic interference (EMI), electromagnetic compatibility (EMC), antenna coverage, and the control of RF radiation hazards. We are looking for self-motivated candidates eager to learn and collaborate to tackle complex problems. The majority of our work takes place at our Pointe-Claire office developing computational simulations with occasional opportunities to travel and participate in shipboard tests and trials.

## Responsibilities

• Developing and maintaining 3D CEM models of shipboard systems;

• Assisting in the computational electromagnetic (CEM) simulation and analysis of antenna and radar systems using state-of-the-art CEM software;

• Processing simulation data;

• Developing expertise with shipboard RF systems;

• Applying and validating EMC standards;

• Preparing and executing shipboard tests and trials;

• Preparing presentation and reports, and,

• Interfacing with our customers.

## Qualifications

• Degree in Electrical Engineering, Physics or equivalent;

• Good understanding and appreciation of electromagnetic and antenna theory;

• Able to work in a small team with shared responsibilities;

• Good writing and communications skills, and

• Must meet the requirements to be eligible for Canadian Security Clearance and Controlled Goods Handling Certification;

Compensation

$85,000-$95,000

