-Canadian Special Operations Regiment;

-Canadian Joint Incident Response Unit;

-Canadian Special Operations Training Center;

-Canadian Special Operations Forces Command Headquarters;

-A Special Operations military organization from Australia, United Kingdom, Canada, United States or New Zealand

• Must have a minimum of 72 months of combined experience within the last 120 months in at least 5 of the following areas:

-Soldier systems equipment (e.g. weapons systems, ammunition, explosives, electro optics equipment, military clothing, personal ballistic protection, load carriage equipment, parachutes);

-Ground vehicles (crewed or uncrewed);

-Air vehicles (crewed or uncrewed);

-Maritime equipment, including crewed or uncrewed crafts;

-Chemical, biological, radiological and nuclear defence equipment;

-Military camp systems (e.g. shelters, electrical power generation and distribution systems, heating, ventilation and air conditioning systems, water purification systems);

-Intelligence, Surveillance and Reconnaissance (ISR);

-Communications;

-Science and technology (e.g. research and development, prototyping, product development) services; and

-Support services, including equipment rentals, facilities and training services.

• Must have a minimum of ninety 96 months combined experience within the last 120 months in the development of technical documents (statements of work (SOW), performance specifications, evaluation plans including bid matrices, and performance trials) for at least 5 of the following areas:

-Soldier systems equipment (e.g. weapons systems, ammunition, explosives, electro optics equipment, military clothing, personal ballistic protection, load carriage equipment, parachutes);

-Ground vehicles (crewed or uncrewed);

-Air vehicles (crewed or uncrewed);

